     width="512" height="512") and positions each of its 9 blobs via its
     own transform="translate(x,y)" - the converter defaulted the
     viewport to a wrong 24x24 and silently dropped every transform
     (same category of bug as the weather icons' dropped <circle>
     elements), which would have rendered all 9 shapes stacked on top of
     each other near the origin and mostly clipped outside a 24-unit
     viewport. Fixed here by setting viewportWidth/Height to the source's
     real 512x512 and wrapping each path in a <group> with the exact
     translateX/Y from its original transform, instead of trying to bake
     the offset into each path's coordinates by hand. -->
